[TestAlertsAbsentVMCheck/absent_over_time_with_a_short_window - 1]
- description: absent_over_time with a short window
  content: |
    - alert: Gone
      expr: absent_over_time(foo{job="a"}[10m])
  output: |
    2 |   expr: absent_over_time(foo{job="a"}[10m])
                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
                `absent_over_time(foo{job="a"}[10m])` returns 1 whenever `foo{job="a"}` has no sample in the
                last 10m. In the last 1w `foo{job="a"}` had 13 pauses of at least 10m on `prom`
                VictoriaMetrics server at https://simple.example.com, the longest at least 1h, while samples
                kept arriving, so this alert fires during normal pauses, not only when `foo{job="a"}`
                disappears.
  problem:
    reporter: alerts/absent
    summary: absent_over_time() window shorter than pauses between samples
    details: vmalert evaluates alerting rules with instant queries. `absent(selector)` returns 1 when the selector has no sample within the query step before the evaluation time, `-datasource.queryStep` of vmalert (5m by default) or `step` from the group `params`, and `absent_over_time(selector[window])` when it has none within the window. A metric written less often than that, for example results of stream aggregation or of batch jobs, makes the alert fire during every pause between samples, and every new sample resets `for`. To alert only when the metric stops, use `absent_over_time(selector[window])` with a window longer than the longest normal pause, or set `for` to at least that long. pint measured the pauses with `count_over_time(selector[window])` over the last 1w, the pause after the last sample isn't counted. It reports pauses that happen at least once a day on average, a single outage isn't reported.
    diagnostics:
        - message: '`absent_over_time(foo{job="a"}[10m])` returns 1 whenever `foo{job="a"}` has no sample in the last 10m. In the last 1w `foo{job="a"}` had 13 pauses of at least 10m on `prom` VictoriaMetrics server at https://simple.example.com, the longest at least 1h, while samples kept arriving, so this alert fires during normal pauses, not only when `foo{job="a"}` disappears.'
          firstcolumn: 1
          lastcolumn: 35
          kind: 0
    lines:
        first: 2
        last: 2
    severity: 1
    anchor: 0

