[TestAlertsAbsentVMCheck/for_shorter_than_the_pauses - 1]
- description: for shorter than the pauses
  content: |
    - alert: Gone
      expr: absent(foo{job="a"})
      for: 20m
  output: |
    2 |   expr: absent(foo{job="a"})
                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
                `absent(foo{job="a"})` returns 1 whenever `foo{job="a"}` has no sample in the last 5m, the
                lookback of vmalert instant queries: the query step, default vmalert -datasource.queryStep
                (5m). In the last 1w `foo{job="a"}` had 13 pauses of at least 5m on `prom` VictoriaMetrics
                server at https://simple.example.com, the longest at least 30m, while samples kept arriving,
                so this alert fires during normal pauses, not only when `foo{job="a"}` disappears. `for:
                20m` covers pauses up to 25m only.
  problem:
    reporter: alerts/absent
    summary: absent() window shorter than pauses between samples
    details: vmalert evaluates alerting rules with instant queries. `absent(selector)` returns 1 when the selector has no sample within the query step before the evaluation time, `-datasource.queryStep` of vmalert (5m by default) or `step` from the group `params`, and `absent_over_time(selector[window])` when it has none within the window. A metric written less often than that, for example results of stream aggregation or of batch jobs, makes the alert fire during every pause between samples, and every new sample resets `for`. To alert only when the metric stops, use `absent_over_time(selector[window])` with a window longer than the longest normal pause, or set `for` to at least that long. pint measured the pauses with `count_over_time(selector[window])` over the last 1w, the pause after the last sample isn't counted. It reports pauses that happen at least once a day on average, a single outage isn't reported.
    diagnostics:
        - message: '`absent(foo{job="a"})` returns 1 whenever `foo{job="a"}` has no sample in the last 5m, the lookback of vmalert instant queries: the query step, default vmalert -datasource.queryStep (5m). In the last 1w `foo{job="a"}` had 13 pauses of at least 5m on `prom` VictoriaMetrics server at https://simple.example.com, the longest at least 30m, while samples kept arriving, so this alert fires during normal pauses, not only when `foo{job="a"}` disappears. `for: 20m` covers pauses up to 25m only.'
